{"name":"Geyser Steam","hex":"#cbd0cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"geyser","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boiling natural spring which throws forth jets of water, mud, etc., at frequent intervals, driven upwards by the expansive power of steam.","A momentary vertical jet or fountain of fluid driven upwards by a violent force."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To (cause to) rush or burst upward like water from a geyser."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geyser"},{"term":"steam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hot gaseous form of water, formed when water changes from the liquid phase to the gas phase (at or above its boiling point temperature).","The suspended condensate (cloud) formed by water vapour when it encounters colder air.\nMist, fog.\nExhaled breath into cold air below the dew point of the exhalation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook with steam.","To be cooked with steam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geyser","blocks":[{"text":"A geyser is a spring with an intermittent water discharge ejected turbulently and accompanied by steam. The formation of geysers is fairly rare and is caused by particular hydrogeological conditions that exist only in a few places on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Yellowstone_National_Park_%28WY%2C_USA%29%2C_Old_Faithful_Geyser_--_2022_--_2599.jpg/330px-Yellowstone_National_Park_%28WY%2C_USA%29%2C_Old_Faithful_Geyser_--_2022_--_2599.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geyser","wikidata":"Q83471"},{"title":"Steam","blocks":[{"text":"Steam is water vapor, often mixed with air and/or an aerosol of liquid water droplets. This may occur by evaporation or by boiling, where heat is applied until water reaches the enthalpy of vaporization. Superheated or saturated steam is invisible; however, wet steam, a visible mist or aerosol of water droplets, is often referred to as \"steam\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg/330px-Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam","wikidata":"Q3251738"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Steamboat_Geyser_in_Yellowstone.jpg/500px-Steamboat_Geyser_in_Yellowstone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Steamboat_Geyser_in_Yellowstone.jpg/1280px-Steamboat_Geyser_in_Yellowstone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Steamboat_Geyser_in_Yellowstone.jpg/500px-Steamboat_Geyser_in_Yellowstone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Steamboat Geyser in Yellowstone National Park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASteamboat_Geyser_in_Yellowstone.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geyser_exploding_1_large.jpg/500px-Geyser_exploding_1_large.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geyser_exploding_1_large.jpg/500px-Geyser_exploding_1_large.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeyser_exploding_1_large.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Geyser_exploding_2_large.jpg/500px-Geyser_exploding_2_large.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Geyser_exploding_2_large.jpg/500px-Geyser_exploding_2_lar